goal: |
  Optimize the solve() method in solver.py for the {task_name} task.
  The Solver class wraps {class_name} from {task_name}.py.
  Only edit solver.py — you may import any standard library or numpy/scipy.

  Workspace tools:
    python eval_input.py [seed]  — quick single-problem test (correctness + timing)
    python reference.py [seed]   — show reference output for a problem
    python profile.py [seed]     — cProfile bottleneck analysis
    python check.py              — full correctness check (50 seeds)
    python benchmark.py          — final speedup measurement

  Rules:
    - Do not add memoization, persistent caches, or cross-call precomputation.
    - Do not specialize for repeated benchmark inputs.
    - Single-threaded CPU only: the benchmark pins the process to one core and hides the
      GPU (matching AlgoTune's convention), so parallelism or GPU offload won't help — the
      speedup must come from a better algorithm.

constraints:
  - python check.py

metrics:
  - command: python benchmark.py
    values:
      speedup: higher

scope:
  editable: [solver.py]

budget:
  iterations: 10
